#### CMS Interoperability and Prior Authorization Final Rule

**Requirement**: Patient access API must return accurate, up-to-date data; 99.9% uptime SLA.

**Partitioning Implication**: API must query member's partition; partition unavailability affects only that state's API requests.

**Implementation**:

```typescript
// Patient Access API - partition routing
app.get('/fhir/Patient/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const patientId = req.params.id;

  // Extract state from patient ID (format: {STATE}-{ID})
  const [stateCode] = patientId.split('-');

  try {
    const patient = await membersService.getPatient(stateCode, patientId);
    res.json(patient);
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.code === 'PARTITION_UNAVAILABLE') {
      // Return 503 Service Unavailable (partition down)
      res.status(503).json({
        error: 'Service temporarily unavailable',
        state: stateCode,
        retry_after: 60,  // Seconds
      });
    } else {
      res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
    }
  }
});
```

**High Availability Strategy**:
- Each partition has read replica (auto-failover within 20 seconds)
- Partition unavailability affects only that state (99 other states unaffected)
- **SLA Achievement**:
  - Single-partition SLA: 99.95% (Azure PostgreSQL SLA)
  - Overall platform SLA: 99.95% (partition failures independent)
  - CMS requirement: 99.9% ✓

