### Example 3: Audit Logs - Range-Based Partitioning

**Scenario**: Partition audit logs (12 billion events over 3 years) by month for efficient querying and data lifecycle management.

**Before Partitioning**:

```text
Single Elasticsearch Cluster:
├─ 12 billion audit events (3-year retention)
├─ Size: 95TB (with replicas)
├─ 24-node cluster
├─ Query performance:
   ├─ Last 24 hours: 2-3 seconds ✓
   ├─ Last 7 days: 8-12 seconds ⚠️
   ├─ Last 30 days: 45-90 seconds (timeout) ❌
   └─ Last 6 months: Not feasible ❌
```

**After Range-Based Partitioning** (PostgreSQL with monthly partitions):

```text
Partitioned Audit Logs:
├─ 36 monthly partitions (3 years × 12 months)
├─ Hot partitions (last 3 months):
   ├─ SSD storage
   ├─ Heavily indexed
   ├─ Size: 8TB

├─ Warm partitions (3-12 months ago):
   ├─ Standard SSD storage
   ├─ Reduced indexes
   ├─ Size: 32TB

├─ Cold partitions (1-3 years ago):
   ├─ HDD storage (Azure Blob cool tier)
   ├─ Minimal indexes
   ├─ Size: 60TB

```

**Implementation**:

```sql
-- PostgreSQL declarative partitioning for audit logs

-- Parent table (partitioned by month)
CREATE TABLE audit_logs (
    log_id BIGSERIAL,
    event_timestamp TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    user_id VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    user_role VARCHAR(50),
    action VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    resource_type VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    resource_id VARCHAR(100),
    state_code VARCHAR(2),
    ip_address INET,
    user_agent TEXT,
    request_id VARCHAR(100),
    session_id VARCHAR(100),
    details JSONB,
    PRIMARY KEY (log_id, event_timestamp)
) PARTITION BY RANGE (event_timestamp);

-- Create monthly partitions (automated script)
-- Hot partitions (last 3 months) - SSD, all indexes
CREATE TABLE audit_logs_2026_01 PARTITION OF audit_logs
    FOR VALUES FROM ('2026-01-01') TO ('2026-02-01')
    TABLESPACE pg_default;  -- SSD tablespace

CREATE INDEX idx_audit_logs_2026_01_user ON audit_logs_2026_01(user_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_logs_2026_01_resource ON audit_logs_2026_01(resource_type, resource_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_logs_2026_01_state ON audit_logs_2026_01(state_code);
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_logs_2026_01_action ON audit_logs_2026_01(action);
CREATE INDEX idx_audit_logs_2026_01_session ON audit_logs_2026_01(session_id);

-- Warm partitions (3-12 months) - Standard SSD, fewer indexes
CREATE TABLE audit_logs_2025_06 PARTITION OF audit_logs
    FOR VALUES FROM ('2025-06-01') TO ('2025-07-01')
    TABLESPACE pg_default;

CREATE INDEX idx_audit_logs_2025_06_user ON audit_logs_2025_06(user_id);
